# FlowDeploy — Operations & Infrastructure Conventions

> Subordinate to `flowdeploy-development-protocol.mdc`.
>
> Scope: how the platform is built, packaged, deployed, versioned, and run — both locally and in production.

---

## 1. Local Development Stack

The `deploy/docker-compose.yml` brings up:

| Service    | Image                        | Purpose                                                                |
| ---------- | ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `traefik`  | `traefik:v3.2`               | Reverse proxy + TLS terminator + gRPC TCP passthrough on `:50051`      |
| `postgres` | `postgres:16-alpine`         | Single Postgres for all backend data (apps, deployments, sessions, …)  |
| `backend`  | built from `apps/backend`    | API + deploy engine + control-plane gRPC (port 8080 HTTP, 50051 gRPC)  |
| `frontend` | built from `apps/frontend`   | Static SPA served behind Traefik on port 80                            |

Network: `paasdeploy` (external — must be created beforehand by `deploy/start.sh`).

Volumes:

- `postgres-data` — Postgres datadir
- `deploy-data` — `/data/apps` mount (cloned repos and per-app filesystem state)
- `traefik-logs`, `traefik-certs`
- `buildkit-cache` — BuildKit cache mounted into the backend at `/var/cache/paasdeploy/buildkit`

Useful commands (root `package.json`):

```bash
pnpm docker:up      # start the stack
pnpm docker:down    # stop the stack
pnpm docker:logs    # follow logs
pnpm docker:build   # rebuild images
```

Start helper: `bash deploy/start.sh` (creates the Docker network, opens ufw port 50051 if applicable, then `docker compose up -d --build`). Stop helper: `bash deploy/stop.sh`.

---

## 2. Traefik

Static config: `deploy/traefik/traefik.yml`. Dynamic config comes from container labels.

Routing in `docker-compose.yml`:

- Backend HTTP: `Host(localhost) && (PathPrefix(/api) || PathPrefix(/events) || PathPrefix(/health))`
- Backend gRPC: TCP entrypoint `grpc` (port 50051) with `tls.passthrough=true` (mTLS terminates at the backend, NOT at Traefik).
- Frontend: `Host(localhost)` (priority 1 so it loses to the backend rule on overlap).

Rules:

- gRPC for the agent ingress MUST stay on TCP passthrough. Don't switch to Traefik HTTP/2 termination — it would break mTLS.
- Don't change the `paasdeploy` network name without updating `start.sh`, the deploy workflow, and any per-app deploy paths.

---

## 3. Database & Migrations

- One Postgres instance per environment.
- Migrations in `apps/backend/migrations/` (golang-migrate, sequence-numbered `NNNNNN_*.{up,down}.sql`).
- Migrations run automatically on backend boot (`runMigrationsFirst()` in `cmd/api/main.go`). DO NOT add a separate "migrate" command — boot is the contract.
- Workflow for a schema change:
  1. Create the next sequential pair (`NNNNNN_description.up.sql`, `.down.sql`).
  2. Update affected `domain.*` types and `repository/*_repository.go`.
  3. Add a Wire provider entry if a new repo is introduced.
  4. Add a corresponding handler/service path if needed.
  5. Run `cd apps/backend && go test ./...` and `pnpm typecheck:frontend` if the API contract changed.
- NEVER modify a migration that has been merged. NEVER renumber.

